<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llotja de la Seda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1482–1533</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Silk Exchange of Valencia, Lonja de la Seda, Valencia Silk Exchange</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Llotja de la Seda, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">Silk</a> Exchange, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> is a late Gothic merchants' exchange whose great hall of twisted columns was built in 1482–1498 under the master Pere Compte, with later wings completed by 1533. It housed the trade in silk and other goods when Valencia was the richest city of the Crown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a>. It has been a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage site since 1996.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llotja-de-la-seda.jpg" alt="Llotja de la Seda" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felivet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llonja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
